AIOps Practical Assessment — Complete Copilot Guide

1. FIRST OPEN THE REPOSITORY — DON'T CHANGE ANYTHING

Since this is an AIOps practical assessment, the safest approach is to use Copilot as a coding/debugging assistant, but you should personally understand and verify every change.

Don't ask Copilot to blindly "complete the whole assessment."

Follow this exact workflow in Codespaces.

Open the GitHub repository in Codespaces.

Then in Copilot Chat, give it this prompt:

"I am working on an AIOps practical assessment.

Do NOT modify any files yet.

First inspect the entire repository and explain:

1. Project structure
2. Purpose of every important file/folder
3. Where operational data is generated/stored
4. Where metrics and logs are handled
5. Where anomaly detection happens
6. Where events are generated
7. Where the producer is implemented
8. What represents the event topic/queue
9. Where the consumer is implemented
10. Where the final AIOps processing/output happens
11. How data flows end-to-end through the project
12. How I should run the complete workflow
13. What tests/validation commands already exist

Also identify the main entry-point files and configuration files.

Do not make any changes. I want to understand the existing architecture first."

IMPORTANT:

Read Copilot's answer yourself.

Compare it with the actual files.


